fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: the_radiant
name: The Radiant
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  level: 5
  role: elite
  armor: 1
  morale: 12              # fearless
  weapon: "Bare hands, offered upward"
  wants: >
    Veier Nolonaire — and to be seen doing it, because worship must be
    witnessed to count. It re-stages the kill if nobody saw.
  special: >
    UNDEFEATABLE — at 0 HP it is not defeated: it removes whoever struck the
    last blow (they drop to 0 HP and are out of the scene), steps into the
    world's shadow, and returns the next exchange at full HP, resuming the
    hunt. A player character it drops to 0 HP takes the Wound, but Hold On can
    go no lower than 7–9. THE HUNT — its errand is Veier; it is faster than
    locked doors but not faster than witnesses. Every exchange in which a
    player character chases, harries, or simply watches it buys Veier another
    hallway. THE LEASH — as the Wept.
  when_bloodied: >
    It re-stages. It steps back into wherever the most eyes are and poses — one
    exchange with no attack at all — then resumes.
  tells: >
    FRACTURE TELLS (one tell: Hard; two or more: Standard). Before midnight:
    makes an antique sign of blessing over the food — Prelate Kovaun
    recognizes the form; lights up when conversation turns to duty, and asks a
    guest, warmly, "Whom do you serve?"; joins the Dead Dance and cannot resist
    dancing beautifully, where the light falls. During the attack: kills are
    staged, offered upward, like rites; it visibly slows and poses when
    watched. In a fight, it turns toward the room before it strikes.
  breaks: >
    Morale never breaks it, and neither does anything else: the Radiant cannot
    be turned from the hunt. It can only be made to feel. FRACTURE — DEVOTION
    (once), a Soul roll by either road: DENY THE CONGREGATION (douse the
    lights, empty the room, turn every back, or a performance that makes
    someone else the better spectacle) or PLANT THE DOUBT (a priest, a
    believer, or anyone armed with what they have seen of its rites, declaring
    to its face that no god worth the name asks for a stolen child). On a 10+
    guilt gets into the errand: it falters at thresholds, looks back,
    re-stages kills — and at the Crossing it does not break past Vell. On a
    7–9 the same, but it answers first with one parting blow or word.
  twists:
  - "A lantern bursts as it passes; the corridor goes dark, and it hurries — nobody is watching."
  - "It stops to stage a kill that is not there — a bystander it has already passed — and loses an exchange."
  - "A crystal charge in a player character's hand goes cold and dark."
  - "It steps through the world's shadow and is ahead of whoever was chasing it."
  - "A door Raunu sealed holds for one exchange longer than it should."
  - "It asks the nearest player character, warmly, whom they serve — and waits for the answer."
  description: >
    A mirror-bright spirit-mask that catches every lamp in the hall. He is a
    person — warm, courtly, genuinely delightful on the subject of duty — who
    blessed his food in a form no priest has used in living memory and joined
    the Dead Dance because he could not help himself. Of the three, he is the
    one who moves like joy — and his kills, when they come, are staged, angled
    toward the room, offered upward. Not showmanship. Liturgy. He believes
    this errand is holy.

    He hunts Veier Nolonaire through corridors that seal themselves behind
    her, and he is losing time he does not have every moment somebody
    WATCHES him.
  notes: >
    Reward pursuit with progress even when rolls fail — failure costs the
    pursuer, not the escape. Guilt is slow, and slow is hallways; the margin at
    the river gate is made of exactly this.

    SHADOW-STEP and UNRAVELING PRESENCE: as the_wept.fof.

    THE CROSSING: at the climax the Radiant is intercepted in the gardens by
    Master Vell — the one being at the ball it is wary of. It breaks past him
    exactly once — unless guilt is already dragging at it, which is what its
    Fracture is for. See module Chapter V.
  organization: >
    One of three. Takes the Dance while the others take the doors and the
    dais.
  reskin_of: null
created_at: '2026-07-12T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00'
